{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788369564895,"sessionID":"ses_f9cdeebfcffeSmuryIjJBGFHi4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a20c0ab4f9677462","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Write app.py with Flask REST API, SQLite, all endpoints + validation","priority":"high","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Write requirements.txt","priority":"high","status":"pending"},{"content":"Write README.md with setup/run instructions","priority":"medium","status":"pending"},{"content":"Write pytest tests (>=3) using Flask test client","priority":"high","status":"pending"},{"content":"Run tests and verify build","priority":"high","status":"pending"}]},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write app.py with Flask REST API, SQLite, all endpoints + validation\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write requirements.txt\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write README.md with setup/run instructions\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write pytest tests (>=3) using Flask test client\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run tests and verify build\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Write app.py with Flask REST API, SQLite, all endpoints + validation","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write requirements.txt","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write README.md with setup/run instructions","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Write pytest tests (>=3) using Flask test client","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run tests and verify build","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"5 todos","time":{"start":1788369564881,"end":1788369564886}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Flask 3.1.3 is now installed along with werkzeug 3.1.8. Flask's test client (which uses werkzeug) is built in, so I can use that for testing without needing requests/httpx.\n\nLet me plan the structure:\n- `app.py` - Flask app with all endpoints, DB init\n- `db.py` - DB helper module\n- `requirements.txt` - flask\n- `README.md` - setup & run\n- `tests/test_books.py` - pytest tests using Flask test client\n\nLet me design the app:\n\n**Database schema:**\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS books (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    title TEXT NOT NULL,\n    author TEXT NOT NULL,\n    year INTEGER,\n    isbn TEXT,\n    created_at TEXT DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n```\n\n**Endpoints:**\n- `GET /health` → `{\"status\": \"healthy\"}` 200\n- `POST /books` → create book. Input: title (required), author (required), year, isbn. Return 201 with created book. 400 if validation fails.\n- `GET /books` → list all books, support `?author=` filter. Return 200 with list.\n- `GET /books/{id}` → get single book. 200 if found, 404 if not.\n- `PUT /books/{id}` → update book. 200 if updated, 404 if not found, 400 if validation fails. Should title/author remain required? For PUT (full update), title and author are required. \n- `DELETE /books/{id}` → delete book. 204 if deleted, 404 if not found.\n\nLet me think about validation. Title and author are required. For PUT (full replacement), they should also be required. Year should be an integer if provided. ISBN is a string.\n\nLet me write a clean, well-structured app. I'll use a single `app.py` for simplicity but also a `db.py` for the database layer. Actually, let me keep it reasonably modular but not over-engineered. I'll do:\n- `app.py` - the Flask application with routes and DB logic\n- `requirements.txt`\n- `README.md`\n- `tests/test_books.py`\n\nLet me create the todo list first since this is a multi-step task.\n\nActually, let me just build it. I'll set up the todos to track progress.\n\nLet me write the app.py. I'll design it so the DB path is configurable via env var (BOOKS_DB_PATH) for testing, defaulting to books.db.\n\nKey design decisions:\n- Use `check_same_thread=False` is not needed since I open a connection per request (better for correctness). Actually, I'll use a connection per request via a helper function `get_db()`. Or I could use Flask's `g` for app context. Let me use a simple approach with a helper that opens/closes a connection.\n\nLet me think about row conversion to dict. I'll set `row_factory = sqlite3.Row` so I can convert to dict easily.\n\nLet me write a helper `query_db` / `execute_db`. Actually simpler to just inline.\n\nLet me write the validation function:\n```python\ndef validate_book(data):\n    errors = []\n    if not data.get(\"title\"):\n        errors.append(\"title is required\")\n    if not data.get(\"author\"):\n        errors.append(\"author is required\")\n    if \"year\" in data and data[\"year\"] is not None:\n        try:\n            int(data[\"year\"])\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            errors.append(\"year must be an integer\")\n    return errors\n```\n\nFor JSON parsing errors, return 400.\n\nLet me write it now. I'll create the files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06321ed74001XY3GU8zr6s0UEK","sessionID":"ses_f9cdeebfcffeSmuryIjJBGFHi4","messageID":"msg_06321a067001t4x38AqQPE5HKr"}}
