{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788369612710,"sessionID":"ses_f9cdeebfcffeSmuryIjJBGFHi4","part":{"id":"prt_06322af9d001a54YW2VEZKfBj1","messageID":"msg_06322a51f001vokiP8sqaqBec2","sessionID":"ses_f9cdeebfcffeSmuryIjJBGFHi4","snapshot":"ea3a76c00d4b393cf5e11a7d794ee26611bf5b42","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788369625027,"sessionID":"ses_f9cdeebfcffeSmuryIjJBGFHi4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-93df22ae29b60bff","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Book Collection REST API\n\nA small REST API service for managing a book collection, written in Python\nwith [Flask](https://flask.palletsprojects.com/) and backed by an embedded\nSQLite database.\n\n## Features\n\n- `POST /books` — Create a new book (`title`, `author`, `year`, `isbn`)\n- `GET /books` — List all books (supports `?author=` filter)\n- `GET /books/{id}` — Retrieve a single book by ID\n- `PUT /books/{id}` — Update a book\n- `DELETE /books/{id}` — Delete a book\n- `GET /health` — Health check endpoint\n\nData is stored in a local SQLite file (`books.db` by default). All responses\nare JSON and use appropriate HTTP status codes. `title` and `author` are\nrequired fields; `year` must be an integer when provided.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python 3.9+\n- Flask\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\n# (optional) create a virtual environment\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n\n# install dependencies\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n## Running the server\n\n```bash\npython app.py\n```\n\nThe server listens on `http://0.0.0.0:5000` by default. Override host/port\nand the database location with environment variables:\n\n```bash\nPORT=8000 HOST=127.0.0.1 BOOKS_DB_PATH=/tmp/books.db python app.py\n```\n\n## Example usage\n\n```bash\n# Create a book\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:5000/books \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"1984\",\"author\":\"George Orwell\",\"year\":1949,\"isbn\":\"978-0451524935\"}'\n\n# List all books\ncurl -s http://localhost:5000/books\n\n# Filter by author\ncurl -s \"http://localhost:5000/books?author=George%20Orwell\"\n\n# Get a single book\ncurl -s http://localhost:5000/books/1\n\n# Update a book\ncurl -s -X PUT http://localhost:5000/books/1 \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"Nineteen Eighty-Four\",\"author\":\"George Orwell\",\"year\":1949}'\n\n# Delete a book\ncurl -s -X DELETE http://localhost:5000/books/1\n```\n\n## Running the tests\n\n```bash\npip install pytest\npytest -q\n```\n\n## Project layout\n\n```\napp.py              # Flask application, routes, SQLite access, validation\nrequirements.txt    # Python dependencies\nREADME.md           # This file\ntests/\n    test_books.py   # Unit / integration tests\n```\n","filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/README.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1788369625014,"end":1788369625023}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_06322afa4001FTPu6oSJE76TmV","sessionID":"ses_f9cdeebfcffeSmuryIjJBGFHi4","messageID":"msg_06322a51f001vokiP8sqaqBec2"}}
